{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I hated.</b> All 'amal' in this book is in the sense of great exertion of effort, as in 'who did not labor in it,' and one departs from it with little effort and nothing. And 'look at 'amal' and rahav, 'amal and aven' — its meaning is: the days of our years are a number; they have a beginning and an end. And the days of dominion and wealth — most of them are 'amal and aven,' and they are the days of youth, and quickly they are cut off and pass away swiftly as though flown away."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The scriptural quotations are given in Hebrew letters without vocalization; I have transliterated rather than supplied missing pointing. The final phrase is hyper-literal; Ibn Ezra's syntax is compressed and elliptical throughout."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:57.318463138Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}